<!--
  ============================================================================
  munction.system.xml — Munction™ Reach-Composition System (BODI™-witnessed)
  ============================================================================

  BODI™ DOCUMENT COMMENT
  ======================
  This document is a BODI™ (Bloq Object Directory Interface) system definition
  for Munction™, SLeeLa's reach-composition fluent form. It is a source
  artifact: the SLeeLa toolchain lowers it into two congruent forms — a Java
  reference surface (com.mearvk.sleela.munction) and a SLeeLa Wrapper™ surface
  (the Munction contextual built-in, syntax 1.3). The document does not execute;
  it declares the addressable Munction™ system — its verb ladder, its
  system-method channels, and its receivability/coherence/receipt contract — so
  both emitted forms remain answerable to one witnessed definition.

  A Munction™ is one sane sentence of reach. Every sentence sits inside the
  BODI™ mitigative circumference: it carries system → reference → change →
  method → sequence → starter → man, and every verb is drawn from the closed
  BODI™ middle-verb ladder (register/bind → connect → open → enable → push →
  attach → pull → observe → propagate → commit → contain → close/unregister).

  BODI™ AUTHORS
  =============
  Author        : Max Rupplin — MEARVK LLC — 2026
  Full name     : Maximilian Eric Alexander Rupplin von Keffikon
  Witness (man) : operator
  Starter       : munction
  Trademarks    : Munction™ (reach-composition form); BODI™; Wrapper™ (.sleela).
  Governance    : MUNCTION.md; BODI.md; NETWORK.md; CONNECTOR.md;
                  SLEELA.syntax (§8 Constitution); munction/COMPILER_NOTE.md.

  BODI™ SYSTEM PREFACE
  ====================
  The structure of Reach is what we protect here. A Munction™ may traverse
  supposed network hatches or bumps and still continue to reach; what it must
  never do is lose the shape of the reach or the truth of the receipt.

  This preface fixes the reading order for everything below:

    1. A Munction™ is an ADDRESSED reach. Its BODI™ address is
       Bodi.system("munction"); the registry reference is urn:sleela:bodi:1.
    2. One SENTENCE, one grammar, every system method. connect() resolves a
       channel from the URI scheme (pipe, file, tcp/http, sdps, crypto); only
       the scheme changes, never the sentence.
    3. RECEIVABLE by construction. Every reach yields a receipt; no consume
       fabricates a reception; no channel that cannot receipt is admitted.
    4. COHERENT send by construction. Every send accounts offered vs.
       acknowledged bytes; a bump that drops bytes is visible, never silent.
    5. SANE and BOUNDED. Between 4 and 16 calls inclusive, a legal verb ladder,
       one opener, one closer. Longer intent is two Munctions joined by a latch
       and a receipt.
    6. WITNESSED. A shape violation is a BODI™ boundary stop recorded in the
       receipt, not meaning invented past the boundary.

  The body is three BODI™ lifecycle containers keyed by mode:
    mode="1" purpose="startup"   — declare + emit the Munction™ system
    mode="2" purpose="runtime"   — the live reach circumference (a sentence)
    mode="3" purpose="shutdown"  — orderly teardown and the receipt
  ============================================================================
-->

<document
    xmlns:bodi="urn:sleela:bodi:1"
    system="munction"
    version="1.0"
    sleela-syntax="1.3"
    conduct-frame="US">

    <preface title="Munction™ Reach-Composition System — BODI™ System Preface">
        <trademark>Munction™ — the reach-composition fluent form</trademark>
        <trademark>BODI™ — Bloq Object Directory Interface</trademark>
        <trademark>Wrapper™ — the .sleela source filetype</trademark>
        <author role="attention">Max Rupplin — MEARVK LLC — 2026</author>
        <author role="full-name">Maximilian Eric Alexander Rupplin von Keffikon</author>
        <bodi:witness
            system="munction"
            reference="urn:sleela:bodi:1"
            sequence="001"
            starter="munction"
            man="operator" />
        <statement>
            A Munction™ is one sane sentence of reach (4..16 calls) over any
            system method. It protects the structure of Reach, is receivable by
            construction, sends coherently, and always closes with a receipt.
        </statement>
    </preface>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         COMPILATION CONTRACT — how this XML becomes Java + SLeeLa.
         Each <emit> is a witnessed BODI™ operation.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <compilation model="1" purpose="xml-to-java-and-sleela">

        <emit target="sleela" verb="install" artifact="Munction (contextual built-in)">
            <bodi:change system="munction" method="install" sequence="010"
                         starter="compiler" man="operator" />
            <pragma>#sleela 1.3</pragma>
            <role>
                A syntax-1.3 contextual built-in. Munction.start(...) is an
                ordinary qualified call and the chain is ordinary fluent
                member-call syntax; no new lexer/parser tokens. Recognized and
                bound at the compiler built-in dispatch point (tryEmitBuiltin),
                and version-gated like the network built-ins (NETWORK.md §10).
            </role>
            <maps-to kind="sleela-builtin">Munction</maps-to>
        </emit>

        <emit target="java" verb="bind" artifact="com.mearvk.sleela.munction">
            <bodi:change system="munction" method="bind" sequence="011"
                         starter="compiler" man="operator" />
            <language-level>Java 25+ (reference surface; forward-compatible)</language-level>
            <role>
                The fluent Munction engine, the MunctionChannel receivability +
                coherent-send contract, the scheme→channel registry, the
                channel implementations, and the witnessed MunctionReceipt.
            </role>
            <maps-to kind="java-package">com.mearvk.sleela.munction</maps-to>
        </emit>

        <congruence verb="observe" rule="strict">
            Verb names, the 4..16 call bound, the legal sequence, the channel
            schemes, and the receipt shape are identical across the Java and
            SLeeLa emits. A verb or scheme present in one and absent in the other
            is rejected at compile time (BODI™ contain), never bridged.
        </congruence>
    </compilation>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         MODE 1 — STARTUP: declare the Munction™ system, its verb ladder,
         its channels, and its receivability/coherence/receipt contract.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <container mode="1" purpose="startup">

        <guard>

            <container
                class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.Munction"
                wrapper="Munction"
                interface="fluent reach sentence">

                <bodi:reference address="urn:sleela:bodi:1" system="munction" />

                <!-- The sanity bound: a sane sentence is 4..16 calls. -->
                <bound min="4" max="16"
                       counts="opener + middles + closer"
                       enforced-at="builder compose-time and compiler gate"
                       on-violation="boundary stop; receipt CONTAINED with a bump" />

                <!-- ============================================================
                     THE VERB LADDER (mapped to BODI™). Positive verbs advance
                     the reach; negative verbs retire it. (MUNCTION.md §3)
                     ============================================================ -->
                <verbs>
                    <verb name="start"            bodi="register+bind" arity="1" role="opener"  once="true" first="true">
                        <intent>Name and open an addressed reach.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="connect"          bodi="connect"       arity="1" role="middle">
                        <intent>Bind the reach to a channel resolved from the URI scheme.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="open"             bodi="open"          arity="0" role="middle" optional="true">
                        <intent>Explicitly open the resource (implied by connect).</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="enable"           bodi="enable"        arity="1" role="middle" repeatable="true">
                        <intent>Permit an optional capability (retry, crypto:&lt;keyref&gt;, compress).</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="send"             bodi="push"          arity="1" role="middle" coherent="true">
                        <intent>Coherently push a datum onto the channel.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="thatch"           bodi="attach"        arity="1" role="middle">
                        <intent>Weave interim stages over the covered path (before the consumes it covers).</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="consume"          bodi="pull"          arity="0" role="middle" repeatable="true">
                        <intent>Pull one available unit of what the channel returns.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="observe"          bodi="observe"       arity="0" role="middle">
                        <intent>Record channel state into the witness without consuming.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="propagate"        bodi="propagate"     arity="1" role="middle" bounded="degree&lt;=4, depth&lt;=3024">
                        <intent>Carry the reach onward to a further endpoint (federated).</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="latch"            bodi="commit"        arity="0" role="middle" once="true">
                        <intent>Hold/commit the reached state so it survives the close.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="contain"          bodi="contain"       arity="0" role="middle">
                        <intent>Stop propagation at the boundary (safe partial close).</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="closeWithReceipt" bodi="close+commit"  arity="0" role="closer" preferred="true" last="true">
                        <intent>Orderly teardown that returns the witnessed receipt.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="close"            bodi="close"         arity="0" role="closer" last="true">
                        <intent>Plain closer; orderly teardown.</intent>
                    </verb>
                    <verb name="abort"            bodi="contain+rollback" arity="0" role="closer" last="true" negative="true">
                        <intent>Negative closer: retire early; the receipt records the residual.</intent>
                    </verb>
                </verbs>

                <!-- The legal sequence the builder and the compiler enforce. -->
                <sequence-rule>
                    start ( connect ( open? enable* ) )
                    ( send | thatch | consume | observe | propagate | latch )+
                    ( closeWithReceipt | close | abort )
                </sequence-rule>

                <!-- ============================================================
                     SYSTEM-METHOD CHANNELS — one grammar reaches all of them.
                     connect(uri) resolves the channel by scheme. (MUNCTION.md §4)
                     ============================================================ -->
                <channels registry="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.MunctionChannels" verb="connect">
                    <channel scheme="pipe" class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.channels.PipeChannel"
                             method="OS pipe / FIFO / stdio" framing="block frames" />
                    <channel scheme="file" class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.channels.FileChannel"
                             method="file I/O" note="send appends; consume reads back" />
                    <channel scheme="tcp|net" class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.channels.NetChannel"
                             method="internet (TCP)" note="NETWORK.md six-primitive TCP layer; bounded read" />
                    <channel scheme="http|https" class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.channels.HttpChannel"
                             method="internet (HTTP)" note="JDK HttpClient; connector HTTP path" />
                    <channel scheme="sdps" class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.channels.PacketChannel"
                             method="private packets (Secure Datum Packet Stream)"
                             framing="magic 'SDPS' + uint32 length + opaque datum + 32-byte MAC" />
                    <channel scheme="crypto" class="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.channels.CryptoChannel"
                             method="crypto envelope" note="wraps an inner channel; seals on send, opens on consume; keyref via enable('crypto:&lt;keyref&gt;'), never in the URI" />
                    <extensible>A new system method is a channel registration (scheme → channel), not a grammar change.</extensible>
                </channels>

                <!-- ============================================================
                     THE CHANNEL CONTRACT — receivability + coherent send.
                     (MUNCTION.md §5) Every channel implements exactly this.
                     ============================================================ -->
                <channel-contract interface="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.MunctionChannel">
                    <op name="scheme"  returns="String" />
                    <op name="open"    returns="void"><param name="address" type="String" /></op>
                    <op name="send"    returns="SendCoherence" coherent="true"><param name="datum" type="byte[]" /></op>
                    <op name="thatch"  returns="void"><param name="interims" type="Interims" /></op>
                    <op name="consume" returns="Reception" receivable="true" />
                    <op name="observe" returns="String" />
                    <op name="latch"   returns="void" />
                    <op name="close"   returns="ChannelReceipt" />
                </channel-contract>

            </container>

        </guard>

    </container>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         MODE 2 — RUNTIME: the live reach circumference (one sentence). Reach
         is protected across network hatches and bumps; sends are coherent,
         receptions are truthful, and the receipt accumulates as the reach runs.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <container mode="2" purpose="runtime">

        <reach system="munction" verb="observe">
            <bodi:reference address="urn:sleela:bodi:1" system="munction.reach" />

            <!-- Reach is the live, shaped path from opener to current verb. -->
            <protected-structure>
                Reach carries: address(name), bound channel, sequence position,
                datum in flight, accumulated interims, and witness. Hatches (NAT,
                proxies, gateways) and bumps (drops, retries, partial reads) may
                perturb transport; the Reach structure is preserved or the chain
                contains at its boundary and records the residual fact.
            </protected-structure>

            <!-- Receivability: every reach can answer "what was received?" and
                 yields a receipt at the close. -->
            <receivability verb="observe">
                <reception model="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.Reception">
                    <field name="present"  type="boolean" note="false at end-of-reach; never fabricated" />
                    <field name="datum"    type="byte[]" />
                    <field name="digest"   type="String" />
                    <field name="sequence" type="long" />
                </reception>
            </receivability>

            <!-- Coherent send: offered vs. acknowledged bytes are accounted. -->
            <coherent-send verb="push">
                <coherence model="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.SendCoherence">
                    <field name="datumDigest"  type="String" />
                    <field name="offered"      type="long" />
                    <field name="acknowledged" type="long" />
                    <field name="coherent"     type="boolean" note="offered == acknowledged, or framing proves full acceptance" />
                </coherence>
            </coherent-send>

            <!-- The receipt accumulates verb by verb; it is the durable proof. -->
            <receipt model="com.mearvk.sleela.munction.MunctionReceipt">
                <field name="name" />       <field name="scheme" />   <field name="address" note="no secrets" />
                <field name="sent" type="List&lt;SendCoherence&gt;" />
                <field name="received" type="List&lt;Reception&gt;" />
                <field name="interims" />   <field name="latched" type="boolean" />
                <field name="outcome" type="REACHED|CONTAINED|ABORTED" />
                <field name="bumps" note="residual facts: retries, partial reads, verify failures" />
                <field name="witness" note="BODI™: system, sequence, verb, datum, boundary, man" />
                <field name="startedAt" /> <field name="closedAt" />
            </receipt>

            <boundary verb="contain">
                A transport success never implies business success; the reply
                status is authoritative. A send that is not acknowledged is not
                claimed; a reception that did not arrive is not fabricated. A
                bump is recorded, and propagation stops at the boundary rather
                than inventing meaning (BODI.md §5).
            </boundary>
        </reach>

    </container>

    <!-- ====================================================================
         MODE 3 — SHUTDOWN: orderly teardown producing the receipt.
         ==================================================================== -->
    <container mode="3" purpose="shutdown">
        <sequence>
            <stop order="1" verb="contain" target="propagation"
                  detail="Stop any onward propagation at the boundary (safe partial close)." />
            <stop order="2" verb="commit"  target="latch"
                  detail="If latched, the reached state is held so it survives the close." />
            <stop order="3" verb="close"   target="channel"
                  detail="MunctionChannel.close() releases the OS resource and yields a ChannelReceipt." />
            <stop order="4" verb="commit"  target="receipt"
                  detail="closeWithReceipt() folds channel receipt + sends + receptions + bumps into the witnessed MunctionReceipt (REACHED | CONTAINED | ABORTED)." />
        </sequence>
        <bodi:witness system="munction" sequence="901" starter="munction" man="operator" />
    </container>

    <!--
      BODI™ CLOSING NOTE
      ==================
      Every verb, channel, send, and reception above declares its address, verb,
      sequence, witness, and boundary. The structure of Reach is protected; the
      receipt is the truth of what was reached. Anything not declared here is
      contained, not invented. — Max Rupplin — MEARVK LLC — 2026. Munction™,
      BODI™, Wrapper™.
    -->

</document>
